Syntax: infuse <item> <essence>

Infuse writes what an essence holds onto a piece of gear.

The essence's quality is what it writes, and the whole essence is spent
however little of it lands -- so grow one to exactly the size you need and
never overshoot.

A piece holds three stats at most.  Its greatest may reach five, its second
four, its third three, and a fourth will not go on at all.  Which is which
is decided by what each stat is worth and not by the order they were
written, so raising one past another takes its place in the order and its
ceiling with it.  The essence costs the same wherever you put it, so a piece
that concentrates on one thing beats a piece spread across three.

No piece can carry two fives.  Reaching five means standing first, and
passing whatever stands there means exceeding your own ceiling to do it.

Writing over a stat already there only ever raises it.  An essence that
would match it or fall short is refused rather than wasted.

Hit points, mana and movement are written in blocks of five and do not count
against the three.

See also: DISTILL, ESSENCE, BOLSTER
